## Shared Web consumption of current Foundation command-path disposition

Shared Web has consumed the Foundation response in comment `5273888120` for the conversational Owner-command path.

Current Web planning consequence:
- existing generic `CON-009` security-context, `CON-002` authority, `CON-004` FIL command envelope, `CON-005` event, and `CON-008` evidence primitives may be treated only according to their current approved semantics;
- authentication remains distinct from authorization;
- Application/plugin admission is not browser/Owner-command admission;
- Shared Web SHALL keep any authority-bearing browser/conversational command path planning-only/fail-closed until the residual Owner authentication/session/high-consequence step-up and generic Web/browser inbound command-admission capability is governed and implemented by Foundation;
- Web AI normalization is transformation only and creates no authority.

This consumes the current Foundation response. A separate Kill-specific follow-up will be posted because the Project Owner has now asked whether Falcon-wide AI Kill behavior has been fully reconciled across Foundation and Applications.

`WEB_CURRENT_COMMAND_PATH_CONSUMPTION = COMPLETE`

## Shared Web consumption ΓÇö Falcon-wide AI Kill Foundation disposition

Shared Web has consumed Foundation disposition comment `5275730184` for current ideas/architecture planning.

Planning result preserved:

- generic Falcon-wide Owner AI emergency containment/Kill is a valid `ACCEPTED_FOR_PLANNING` Foundation requirement;
- the unified generic Kill Enforcer/runtime/control plane is currently `MISSING` and `UNASSIGNED`;
- existing Foundation Authority/Lifecycle/Guardian/Security/Evidence/Recovery capabilities are reusable partial building blocks, not a complete Kill implementation;
- authoritative Kill Enforcer/control-plane ownership remains Foundation-owned; Shared Web, the mobile emergency client, target AI, and target Application do not become Kill authority;
- blast-radius/target-selection, independent Owner path outside Shared Web/target control, complete mobile emergency security/status composition, and end-to-end runtime composition remain unresolved/partial as recorded by Foundation;
- logical/control-plane independence from the target is required by current Owner intent; physical/out-of-band hardware is not inferred as mandatory without a later governed decision;
- FSA-specific Factory Reset / Controlled Revival details remain governed by FCR-0012 and shall not be generalized Falcon-wide by implication;
- no implementation/runtime/deployment authority is created.

Shared Web will therefore continue only conceptual/UX planning and will fail closed on any claim that the Falcon-wide Kill path is implementation-ready until Foundation assigns, governs, implements and evidences the residual generic capability.

`HANDOFF_UPDATE_REQUIRED: Waiting On=NONE; Next Required Action=No immediate cross-workstream action during ideas/discussion. Preserve the Foundation disposition and re-review/return a bounded FCR before emergency-control architecture freeze or implementation-readiness, when Foundation assigns the residual generic Kill Stage/WP, or after relevant Foundation control/security/recovery capability change; Target Foundation Stage/WP=UNASSIGNED / REQUIRES_GOVERNED_PLANNING for generic Falcon-wide Owner AI emergency containment/Kill; Review Trigger=before emergency-control architecture freeze or implementation-readiness, Foundation Stage/WP assignment, or relevant Foundation capability change.`
